---
description: Carousels show one slide at a time from a set, with previous and next controls.
---

<script>
  import {
    BigNumber,
    Button,
    Carousel,
    CarouselItem,
    Link,
    Stack,
    Tag,
    Tile,
    UserAvatar,
  } from "carbon-components-svelte";
  import ContinuousDelivery from "carbon-pictograms-svelte/lib/ContinuousDelivery.svelte";
  import Dashboard from "carbon-pictograms-svelte/lib/Dashboard.svelte";
  import Rocket from "carbon-pictograms-svelte/lib/Rocket.svelte";
  import Security from "carbon-pictograms-svelte/lib/Security.svelte";
</script>

## Basic

Wrap each slide in a `CarouselItem`. Only the active slide is visible, and the
previous and next buttons are disabled on the first and last slide; the
carousel does not wrap around. When focus is inside the carousel, press <DocKbd label="Left" />
and <DocKbd label="Right" /> to move to the previous and next slide, except
inside form fields, which keep their own arrow key behavior.

<Carousel labelText="What's new in 4.2">
  <CarouselItem>
    <Stack gap={3}>
      <div><Tag type="green" size="sm">New</Tag></div>
      <h4>Scheduled deployments</h4>
      <p>Queue a release for a maintenance window and it ships automatically, with a rollback point created five minutes before it starts.</p>
      <Link href="#scheduled-deployments">Read the release notes</Link>
    </Stack>
  </CarouselItem>
  <CarouselItem>
    <Stack gap={3}>
      <div><Tag type="blue" size="sm">Improved</Tag></div>
      <h4>Faster log search</h4>
      <p>Queries across 30 days of logs now return in under two seconds, and saved searches can be pinned to a dashboard.</p>
      <Link href="#log-search">Try log search</Link>
    </Stack>
  </CarouselItem>
  <CarouselItem>
    <Stack gap={3}>
      <div><Tag type="purple" size="sm">Beta</Tag></div>
      <h4>Cost anomaly alerts</h4>
      <p>Get notified when a service's daily spend moves more than 20% from its 14-day baseline.</p>
      <Link href="#cost-alerts">Join the beta</Link>
    </Stack>
  </CarouselItem>
</Carousel>

## Usage

| Do | Why |
| --- | --- |
| Use a carousel for a short, ordered set of related content, such as release highlights or a first-run tour. | Only one slide is visible at a time, so content the user must compare side by side belongs in a grid or table. |
| Keep the set small, typically three to five slides. | There is no slide picker; reaching the last slide takes one press per slide. |
| Put a call to action on the slide it belongs to. | The prev/next buttons only move between slides; they do not confirm or submit anything. |
| Set `labelText` to describe the set, for example "What's new in 4.2". | Screen readers announce the region as a carousel with this name. |

## Content

Slides accept any markup. Combine them with other components to fit the
context the carousel sits in.

### Feature tour

Pair a pictogram with short copy for a first-run tour, and end on the slide
that starts the task.

<Carousel labelText="Getting started">
  <CarouselItem>
    <Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={6} align="center">
      <Rocket />
      <Stack gap={3}>
        <h4>Deploy from any branch</h4>
        <p>Connect a repository and every push to a branch gets its own preview URL.</p>
      </Stack>
    </Stack>
  </CarouselItem>
  <CarouselItem>
    <Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={6} align="center">
      <ContinuousDelivery />
      <Stack gap={3}>
        <h4>Promote with confidence</h4>
        <p>Promote a preview to production once checks pass. Every promotion can be rolled back in one click.</p>
      </Stack>
    </Stack>
  </CarouselItem>
  <CarouselItem>
    <Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={6} align="center">
      <Security />
      <Stack gap={3}>
        <h4>Secrets stay secret</h4>
        <p>Environment variables are encrypted at rest and only exposed to the environments you choose.</p>
      </Stack>
    </Stack>
  </CarouselItem>
  <CarouselItem>
    <Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={6} align="center">
      <Dashboard />
      <Stack gap={3}>
        <h4>You're all set</h4>
        <p>Create your first project to see builds, logs, and usage in one place.</p>
        <div><Button size="small">Create project</Button></div>
      </Stack>
    </Stack>
  </CarouselItem>
</Carousel>

### Metrics

Cycle through key metrics in a space that only fits one. Each slide is
labeled "Slide N of M" by default; set `label` on a `CarouselItem` to name it
after its content instead.

<Tile>
  <Carousel labelText="Service health" prevButtonLabelText="Previous metric" nextButtonLabelText="Next metric">
    <CarouselItem label="Requests">
      <BigNumber labelText="Requests (24h)" value={1843200} size="lg" trend="up" />
    </CarouselItem>
    <CarouselItem label="Latency">
      <BigNumber labelText="p95 latency (ms)" value={212} size="lg" trend="down" trendColor="success" />
    </CarouselItem>
    <CarouselItem label="Error rate">
      <BigNumber labelText="Error rate" value={0.4} percentage size="lg" trend="flat" />
    </CarouselItem>
  </Carousel>
</Tile>

## Height

By default, the viewport is sized to the tallest slide so the controls stay
put while slides of different lengths cycle through.

<Carousel labelText="Customer stories">
  <CarouselItem>
    <Stack gap={4}>
      <p>"We cut our release cycle from two weeks to two days."</p>
      <Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={3} align="center">
        <UserAvatar name="Priya Raman" size="sm" />
        <span>Priya Raman, Platform Lead at Northwind</span>
      </Stack>
    </Stack>
  </CarouselItem>
  <CarouselItem>
    <Stack gap={4}>
      <p>"Before the migration, every deploy meant a late night and a runbook nobody trusted. Now previews catch most regressions before review, rollbacks take seconds, and on-call has gone from the most dreaded rotation on the team to one people barely notice."</p>
      <Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={3} align="center">
        <UserAvatar name="Tomás Ferreira" size="sm" />
        <span>Tomás Ferreira, SRE at Contoso</span>
      </Stack>
    </Stack>
  </CarouselItem>
  <CarouselItem>
    <Stack gap={4}>
      <p>"Onboarding a new engineer takes an afternoon, not a week."</p>
      <Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={3} align="center">
        <UserAvatar name="Amara Okafor" size="sm" />
        <span>Amara Okafor, Engineering Manager at Fabrikam</span>
      </Stack>
    </Stack>
  </CarouselItem>
</Carousel>

Set `useMaxHeight` to `false` to size the viewport to the active slide
instead. The controls then move with the content, so use it where the
carousel is the last thing in its container.

<Carousel labelText="Customer stories" useMaxHeight={false}>
  <CarouselItem>
    <p>"We cut our release cycle from two weeks to two days."</p>
  </CarouselItem>
  <CarouselItem>
    <p>"Before the migration, every deploy meant a late night and a runbook nobody trusted. Now previews catch most regressions before review, rollbacks take seconds, and on-call has gone from the most dreaded rotation on the team to one people barely notice."</p>
  </CarouselItem>
  <CarouselItem>
    <p>"Onboarding a new engineer takes an afternoon, not a week."</p>
  </CarouselItem>
</Carousel>

## Selection

Choose which slide is active, and read or drive it from outside the carousel.

### Initial slide

Set `selectedIndex` to start on a slide other than the first, for example to
resume a checklist where the user left off. Out-of-range values are clamped
to the first or last slide.

<Carousel labelText="Account setup checklist" selectedIndex={2}>
  <CarouselItem>
    <Stack gap={3}>
      <div><Tag type="green" size="sm">Done</Tag></div>
      <h4>Verify your email</h4>
      <p>Confirmed on March 4.</p>
    </Stack>
  </CarouselItem>
  <CarouselItem>
    <Stack gap={3}>
      <div><Tag type="green" size="sm">Done</Tag></div>
      <h4>Add a payment method</h4>
      <p>Visa ending in 4242.</p>
    </Stack>
  </CarouselItem>
  <CarouselItem>
    <Stack gap={3}>
      <div><Tag type="red" size="sm">Required</Tag></div>
      <h4>Turn on two-factor authentication</h4>
      <p>Protect your account with an authenticator app or a security key.</p>
      <div><Button size="small">Set up 2FA</Button></div>
    </Stack>
  </CarouselItem>
  <CarouselItem>
    <Stack gap={3}>
      <div><Tag type="gray" size="sm">Optional</Tag></div>
      <h4>Invite your team</h4>
      <p>Add collaborators now or later from project settings.</p>
    </Stack>
  </CarouselItem>
</Carousel>

### Two-way binding

Bind `selectedIndex` to keep the carousel in sync with another control. Here,
a `ProgressIndicator` tracks the active step and moves the carousel when a
completed step is clicked. Arrow keys typed in the text input and radio
buttons stay in those fields instead of changing the slide.

<FileSource src="/framed/Carousel/CarouselWizard" />

## Dynamic slides

Add or remove `CarouselItem`s with `{#each}` or `{#if}`. The carousel keeps
the active index, clamps it if the last slide is removed, and renumbers the
default slide labels.

<FileSource src="/framed/Carousel/CarouselAnnouncements" />

## Events

Listen for `change` to react to navigation from the buttons, arrow keys, or a
bound `selectedIndex`. `event.detail` contains `currentIndex`,
`previousIndex`, and `totalViews`. It does not fire for the initial
`selectedIndex`.

<FileSource src="/framed/Carousel/CarouselChange" />
